    "markdown": "![Hugging Face's logo](https://huggingface.co/front/assets/huggingface_logo-noborder.svg) Hugging Face⟨1⟩\n  *  Models ⟨2⟩\n  *  Datasets ⟨3⟩\n  *  Spaces ⟨4⟩\n  *  Buckets new⟨5⟩\n  *  Docs ⟨6⟩\n  *  Enterprise ⟨7⟩\n  * Pricing⟨8⟩\n  *     * Website\n      *  Tasks⟨9⟩\n      *  HuggingChat⟨10⟩\n      *  Collections⟨11⟩\n      *  Languages⟨12⟩\n      *  Organizations⟨13⟩\n    * Community\n      *  Blog⟨14⟩\n      *  Posts⟨15⟩\n      *  Daily Papers⟨16⟩\n      *  Hardware⟨17⟩\n      *  Learn⟨18⟩\n      *  Discord⟨19⟩\n      *  Forum⟨20⟩\n      *  GitHub⟨21⟩\n    * Solutions\n      *  Team & Enterprise⟨7⟩\n      *  Hugging Face PRO⟨22⟩\n      *  Enterprise Support⟨23⟩\n      *  Inference Providers⟨24⟩\n      *  Inference Endpoints⟨25⟩\n      *  Storage Buckets⟨5⟩\n  * * * *\n  * Log In⟨26⟩\n  * Sign Up⟨27⟩\n\n\n# \n ![](https://huggingface.co/avatars/96d91acff1446ffd7dbeb6ad416f6489.svg) ⟨28⟩\ncapital-connect-africa⟨28⟩\n/\nQwen3.5-4B-GGFU⟨29⟩\nlike 0\n GGUF ⟨30⟩ conversational ⟨31⟩\nLicense: mit\n Model card ⟨29⟩ Files Files and versions xet ⟨32⟩ Community ⟨33⟩\nDeploy\nCopy to bucket new\nUse this model\n### Instructions to use capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU with libraries, inference providers, notebooks, and local apps. Follow these links to get started.\n  * Libraries\n  *  llama-cpp-python⟨34⟩\nHow to use capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU with llama-cpp-python:\n\n```\n# !pip install llama-cpp-python\n\nfrom llama_cpp import Llama\n\nllm = Llama.from_pretrained(\n\trepo_id=\"capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU\",\n\tfilename=\"Qwen3.5-4B-Q4_K_M.gguf\",\n)\n\n```\n\n```\nllm.create_chat_completion(\n\tmessages = \"No input example has been defined for this model task.\"\n)\n```\n\n  * Notebooks\n  *  Google Colab⟨35⟩\n  *  Kaggle⟨36⟩\n  * Local Apps Settings⟨37⟩\n  *  llama.cpp ⟨38⟩\nHow to use capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU with llama.cpp:\n##### Install (macOS, Linux)\n\n```\ncurl -LsSf https://llama.app/install.sh | sh\n# Start a local OpenAI-compatible server with a web UI:\nllama serve -hf capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\n# Run inference directly in the terminal:\nllama cli -hf capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Install from WinGet (Windows)\n\n```\nwinget install llama.cpp\n# Start a local OpenAI-compatible server with a web UI:\nllama serve -hf capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\n# Run inference directly in the terminal:\nllama cli -hf capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Use pre-built binary\n\n```\n# Download pre-built binary from:\n# https://github.com/ggerganov/llama.cpp/releases\n# Start a local OpenAI-compatible server with a web UI:\n./llama-server -hf capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\n# Run inference directly in the terminal:\n./llama-cli -hf capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Build from source code\n\n```\ngit clone https://github.com/ggerganov/llama.cpp.git\ncd llama.cpp\ncmake -B build\ncmake --build build -j --target llama-server llama-cli\n# Start a local OpenAI-compatible server with a web UI:\n./build/bin/llama-server -hf capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\n# Run inference directly in the terminal:\n./build/bin/llama-cli -hf capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Use Docker\n\n```\ndocker model run hf.co/capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n  *  LM Studio ⟨39⟩\n  *  Jan ⟨40⟩\n  *  Ollama ⟨41⟩\nHow to use capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU with Ollama:\n\n```\nollama run hf.co/capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n  *  Unsloth Studio ⟨42⟩\nHow to use capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU with Unsloth Studio:\n##### Install Unsloth Studio (macOS, Linux, WSL)\n\n```\ncurl -fsSL https://unsloth.ai/install.sh | sh\n# Run unsloth studio\nunsloth studio -H 0.0.0.0 -p 8888\n# Then open http://localhost:8888 in your browser\n# Search for capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU to start chatting\n```\n\n##### Install Unsloth Studio (Windows)\n\n```\nirm https://unsloth.ai/install.ps1 | iex\n# Run unsloth studio\nunsloth studio -H 0.0.0.0 -p 8888\n# Then open http://localhost:8888 in your browser\n# Search for capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU to start chatting\n```\n\n##### Using HuggingFace Spaces for Unsloth\n\n```\n# No setup required\n# Open https://huggingface.co/spaces/unsloth/studio in your browser\n# Search for capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU to start chatting\n```\n\n  *  Pi ⟨43⟩\nHow to use capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU with Pi:\n##### Start the llama.cpp server\n\n```\n# Install llama.cpp:\nbrew install llama.cpp\n# Start a local OpenAI-compatible server:\nllama serve -hf capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Configure the model in Pi\n\n```\n# Install Pi:\nnpm install -g @mariozechner/pi-coding-agent\n# Add to ~/.pi/agent/models.json:\n{\n  \"providers\": {\n    \"llama-cpp\": {\n      \"baseUrl\": \"http://localhost:8080/v1\",\n      \"api\": \"openai-completions\",\n      \"apiKey\": \"none\",\n      \"models\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n##### Run Pi\n\n```\n# Start Pi in your project directory:\npi\n```\n\n  *  Hermes Agent new⟨44⟩\nHow to use capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU with Hermes Agent:\n##### Start the llama.cpp server\n\n```\n# Install llama.cpp:\nbrew install llama.cpp\n# Start a local OpenAI-compatible server:\nllama serve -hf capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Configure Hermes\n\n```\n# Install Hermes:\ncurl -fsSL https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/install.sh | bash\nhermes setup\n# Point Hermes at the local server:\nhermes config set model.provider custom\nhermes config set model.base_url http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1\nhermes config set model.default capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Run Hermes\n\n```\nhermes\n```\n\n  *  Atomic Chat new⟨45⟩\n  *  OpenClaw new⟨46⟩\nHow to use capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU with OpenClaw:\n##### Start the llama.cpp server\n\n```\n# Install llama.cpp:\nbrew install llama.cpp\n# Start a local OpenAI-compatible server:\nllama serve -hf capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Configure OpenClaw\n\n```\n# Install OpenClaw:\nnpm install -g openclaw@latest\n# Register the local server and set it as the default model:\nopenclaw onboard --non-interactive --mode local \\\n  --auth-choice custom-api-key \\\n  --custom-base-url http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1 \\\n  --custom-model-id \"capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\" \\\n  --custom-provider-id llama-cpp \\\n  --custom-compatibility openai \\\n  --custom-text-input \\\n  --accept-risk \\\n  --skip-health\n```\n\n##### Run OpenClaw\n\n```\nopenclaw agent --local --agent main --message \"Hello from Hugging Face\"\n```\n\n  *  Docker Model Runner ⟨47⟩\nHow to use capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU with Docker Model Runner:\n\n```\ndocker model run hf.co/capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n  *  Lemonade ⟨48⟩\nHow to use capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU with Lemonade:\n##### Pull the model\n\n```\n# Download Lemonade from https://lemonade-server.ai/\nlemonade pull capital-connect-africa/Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Run and chat with the model\n\n```\nlemonade run user.Qwen3.5-4B-GGFU-Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### List all available models\n\n```\nlemonade list\n```\n\n\n\nREADME.md exists but content is empty.  \n\nDownloads last month\n    39\nGGUF⟨49⟩\nModel size\n4B params\nArchitecture\nqwen35\nChat template\nHardware compatibility\nLog In⟨50⟩ to add your hardware\n4-bit\nQ4_K_M 2.78 GB\nInference Providers NEW⟨51⟩\nThis model isn't deployed by any Inference Provider. 🙋 Ask for provider support⟨52⟩\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨53⟩ Privacy⟨54⟩ About⟨55⟩ Careers⟨56⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\nInference providers allow you to run i